    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43728" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septem-gĕmĭnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sevenfold</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nilus (as having seven mouths),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					11, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6, 800</span></i> (cf. the preced. art.
			and septemplex): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Roma (the city of seven hills),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 2, 191</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septemgemino Roma jugo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 1, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
